{"cluster_id": "C-4517", "topic": "stale-metadata cache kill switch", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B008-096", "B039-080"], "canonical_claim": "Operators should set `cas_part_folder_cache_bytes = 0` before investigating suspected stale CAS metadata and run `fsck` or integrity probes with retained views disabled or strict validation enabled. Additionally, For suspected stale metadata, the operational kill switch is `cas_part_folder_cache_bytes = 0`; `fsck` and integrity probes should use `StrictValidate`, which never consults retained views.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/cache.md#operational-risks", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#observability"]}
